       "Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP): legal in India since the 1971 Act; one doctor's opinion up to 20 weeks, two doctors' for 20–24 weeks.",
       "STDs: gonorrhoea, syphilis, genital herpes, chlamydiasis, trichomoniasis, HIV/AIDS — early treatment prevents complications like infertility.",
       "Infertility: failure to conceive after 2 years of unprotected intercourse; causes — male (sperm count/motility), female (ovulation disorders, tubal blockage).",
       "Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART): IVF (test-tube baby), ZIFT, IUT, GIFT, ICSI, artificial insemination (AI) — options for infertile couples."
