       "Increasing function: f′(x) > 0; decreasing function: f′(x) < 0 (in the given interval).",
       "Maxima/minima: points with f′(c) = 0 are critical points; second derivative test — f″(c) < 0 gives maxima, f″(c) > 0 gives minima.",
       "Equation of tangent: y − y1 = f′(x1)(x − x1); slope of normal = −1/f′(x1).",
       "Approximation: Δy ≈ f′(x)·Δx — estimating small changes.",
       "Word problems (maximum area/volume): form the function, find critical points from f′ = 0, then verify with f″.",
       "Tangent: slope of tangent to y=f(x) at (x₀,y₀) = dy/dx|₀; equation: y−y₀ = m(x−x₀).",
       "Normal: perpendicular to tangent; slope = −1/m (m≠0); equation: y−y₀ = −(1/m)(x−x₀).",
       "Angle between two curves: tan θ = |(m₁−m₂)/(1+m₁m₂)|; orthogonal ⇔ m₁m₂=−1.",
       "Increasing/decreasing: f'(x)>0 ⇒ strictly increasing; f'(x)<0 ⇒ strictly decreasing (on an interval).",
       "Monotonic: increasing or decreasing; f'(x)≥0 ⇒ increasing, f'(x)≤0 ⇒ decreasing.",
       "Critical points: f'(x)=0 or undefined; maxima/minima occur here.",
       "First derivative test: f' changes +→− : local maximum; −→+ : local minimum.",
       "Second derivative test: at f'(c)=0, f''(c)<0 ⇒ maximum; f''(c)>0 ⇒ minimum; =0 ⇒ inconclusive.",
       "Point of inflection: f''(x) changes sign — direction of concavity changes.",
       "Absolute maxima/minima: on closed [a,b], compare f(a), f(b) and critical values.",
       "Maxima–minima problems: eliminate a variable using the second-derivative-zero condition, then test.",
       "Rate of change: dy/dt = (dy/dx)(dx/dt); related rates — sphere, cone volumes.",
       "Approximation: Δy ≈ f'(x)Δx; for approximate √ and cube-root values.",
       "f(x)=x³−3x: f'=3x²−3=0 ⇒ x=±1; x=−1 maximum, x=1 minimum.",
       "Maximum area: square/circle for fixed perimeter; cylinder for fixed volume.",
       "Max–min values: after f'' test compare with endpoint values (if interval is open).",
       "Normal parallel to x-axis ⇔ tangent parallel to y-axis (for m=0 the normal is vertical).",
       "Tangent to y=x² at (1,1): y−1=2(x−1) ⇒ y=2x−1; normal: y−1=−(x−1)/2.",
       "Concavity: f''>0 concave up, f''<0 concave down — basis of the max/min test.",
       "Economics: marginal cost = C'(x), marginal revenue = R'(x); profit max where R'=C'."
