       "Differential equation: equation with independent variable, dependent variable and derivatives; e.g. dy/dx + y = x.",
       "Order: order of the highest derivative; degree: power of the highest derivative (in polynomial form).",
       "For degree to be defined, derivatives must not be in fractions/roots; d²y/dx² + (dy/dx)³ = 0: order 2, degree 1.",
       "dy/dx + sin(dy/dx) = 0: degree not defined (not polynomial).",
       "General solution: number of arbitrary constants = order; particular solution: constants given values.",
       "Forming a DE: n constants → differentiate n times to eliminate them.",
       "Variable separable: dy/dx = f(x)g(y) ⇒ dy/g(y) = f(x)dx — integrate both sides.",
       "Homogeneous: dy/dx = F(y/x) — put y=vx to make it separable.",
       "Linear: dy/dx + Py = Q (P,Q functions of x); integrating factor IF = e^∫Pdx.",
       "Solution: y·IF = ∫Q·IF dx + C — standard formula.",
       "dx/dy + P₁x = Q₁ (x dependent): IF = e^∫P₁dy — y is the independent variable.",
       "Family of curves: y = mx (m constant) ⇒ dy/dx = y/x (order 1); y = Ax²+Bx ⇒ order 2.",
